The class `BlockingMultiObserver` is a thin synchronization wrapper around RxJava's observer interfaces, primarily delegating to `CountDownLatch` and handling disposables. Its methods (`blockingGet`, `blockingAwait`, `blockingConsume`) are simple coordination utilities rather than computationally intensive logic. Benchmarking such thin wrappers with JMH would provide limited insight, as performance is dominated by the underlying RxJava infrastructure and thread scheduling rather than the code in this class itself. Therefore, generating JMH benchmarks for this class is unnecessary.